  "notes": "The pop-punk crossover reference: 140–175 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 at speed, and the signature single is exactly 150 in common time, which is where `bpm.mode` sits. The harmonic policy is documented rather than inferred — C major with **I–IV–V and nothing else**, \"diatonic major-key movement and simple chord relationships\", with an occasional vi for a bridge — so three short families, a triad share of 0.82 and no extensions worth the name. The drum block is defined by an absence the research states outright: \"**ghost-note-free, all accents**\", which is why `ghost.prob` is 0.02, the lowest in this section, against a very loud tier. The other deltas are \"8th-note kick under the chorus\" (a 4–8 density with the four anchors), \"hat 8ths in verse and crash-8ths in the chorus\", and \"skate-punk fills = a 16th snare-to-tom run of one bar\", which is the crash/tom perc block with a 16th snare-roll ladder. The bass \"follows the guitar exactly\" with \"no fills\" and \"carries the verse alone when the guitars drop\": `mirror_kick` at 0.98. The melody is documented as G4–F5 — \"a narrow, nasal, single-octave band\" — with \"'na-na' gang hooks\", so the register is exactly that and the counter is a plain octave echo. The arrangement is the entry's too: \"no pre-chorus\", 8-bar choruses, a bridge that drops to bass-and-hat, and songs under three minutes. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and the melody density.",
